Confirmed: a modified line `two\n` → `HELLO\n` produces a single hunk with buffer row range 1..2 (i.e. rows 1 to before 2), so `buffer_range` as Point is (1,0)..(2,0). This matches my hand computation for the practice task.

Note in the second part of the test: `buffer.edit([(0..0, "point five\n")])` then `new_sync` again — but that recomputes from scratch. For my practice I want to demonstrate the *stale snapshot* path: create diff via new_sync, then edit the buffer WITHOUT recomputing, then call patch_for_buffer_range / point mapping functions with the *current* buffer snapshot — this exercises the edits_since composition. That's the whole point of this lecture. 

Let me design the practice test carefully:

```rust
#[gpui::test]
async fn test_point_mapping_practice(cx: &mut gpui::TestAppContext) {
    let base_text = "one\ntwo\nthree\nfour\n";
    let buffer_text = "one\nTWO\nthree\nfour\n";

    let mut buffer = Buffer::new(ReplicaId::LOCAL, BufferId::new(1).unwrap(), buffer_text);
    let diff = BufferDiffSnapshot::new_sync(&buffer, base_text.to_string(), cx);

    // —— 第一部分：未再编辑时，映射是"纯 hunk 编辑"的效果 ——
    // hunk: buffer 行区间 (1,0)..(2,0)，base 字节区间 4..8
    assert_eq!(
        diff.buffer_point_to_base_text_point(Point::new(0, 2), &buffer),
        Point::new(0, 2) // hunk 之前的区域：恒等映射
    );
    assert_eq!(
        diff.buffer_point_to_base_text_point(Point::new(1, 1), &buffer),
        Point::new(1, 0) // 落在 hunk 内部：折叠到 hunk 的 base 起点
    );
    assert_eq!(
        diff.buffer_point_to_base_text_point(Point::new(2, 0), &buffer),
        Point::new(2, 0) // 恰好等于 hunk 的 old.end：返回 new.end
    );

    assert_eq!(
        diff.base_text_point_to_buffer_point(Point::new(1, 1), &buffer),
        Point::new(1, 0)
    );
    assert_eq!(
        diff.base_text_point_to_buffer_point(Point::new(3, 0), &buffer),
        Point::new(3, 0)
    );

    // —— 第二部分：diff 之后又编辑 buffer ——
